From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: fe13 <engine@localhost>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 03:20:04 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 02/21] gpu: pieces of the bottom screen over the top one, and
 the bottom screen over it

Two layouts the frontend can pick while the top screen shows alone:
TopWithPieces (parts of the bottom screen drawn over the top one as rounded
rectangles, placed by piece_places) and BottomOverTop (the whole bottom
screen over the middle of the top one). The presenters draw neither: the
overlay does, through BOTTOM_SCREEN_TEXTURE, an overlay texture id both
presenters (Vulkan, OpenGL) map to the bottom screen's picture. cut_out finds
a part's outline on its background in a 320x240 picture.

Nothing changes for the existing layouts.

Adapted from fe-awakening-recomp 832fe86 (github.com/Zelkin1/fe-awakening-recomp,
MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 the authors of the Fire Emblem: Awakening
recompilation project), patches/zakuro-local-changes.patch: backend/mod.rs,
gl.rs, vulkan.rs, vulkan_overlay.rs. Fitted to Zakuro 0.2.32's screen
rotation (the bottom-over viewport is placed before rotation and offset).
